Description: Open source RGB lighting control
 OpenRGB controls the RGB lighting of motherboards, memory, graphics cards,
 coolers, keyboards, mice and other peripherals from many vendors, without
 each vendor's own software. It has a Qt interface, a command line, and an
 SDK server for other programs.
 .
 This is OpenRGB 1.0 built from the project's own release
 (https://gitlab.com/CalcProgrammer1/OpenRGB, tag release_1.0).
 .
 What this package installs: the program, its desktop entry and icon, a
 udev rules file (/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/60-openrgb.rules) generated at build
 time by the program itself from its list of supported USB devices, so that
 a normal user can reach them, and the project's systemd unit for the SDK
 server, which is NOT enabled or started. It loads no kernel module and
 sets no kernel parameter. Devices on the SMBus (RGB memory, some
 motherboards) need the i2c-dev module and the chipset's i2c driver, which
 the hardware setup of the system provides when it finds such hardware.
 .
 Warning from the project: OpenRGB talks to hardware through reverse
 engineered protocols; there have been cases of damaged devices. Use is at
 your own risk.
